            "text": "A major international news headline for today, August 8, 2026, involves an escalation of tensions in the Middle East following a reported attack on a commercial vessel.\n\n### **Top Headline: UAE accuses Iran of missile attack on vessel in Strait of Hormuz**\nThe United Arab Emirates has officially condemned what it described as a \"hostile Iranian attack\" on an oil tanker linked to the state-owned **ADNOC** company. The vessel was reportedly targeted by a missile early Saturday morning as it transited the **Strait of Hormuz**. The UAE has characterized the incident as an \"act of piracy\" and a violation of UN Security Council resolutions regarding the freedom of navigation. While no injuries were reported, the event has caused immediate concern for global oil and liquefied natural gas shipping routes.\n\n**Source:** [Al-Monitor](https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/08/uae-says-iran-attacked-adnoc-vessel-missile-strait-hormuz) (citing Reuters)\n\n---\n\n### **Other Top Stories for August 8, 2026:**\n*   **U.S. Senate Passes Sanctions:** In an 86-11 vote, the U.S. Senate passed the **\"Lindsey O. Graham Sanctioning Russia and Iran Act of 2026,\"** a sweeping bill aimed at increasing economic pressure on Moscow and Tehran. The legislation, named after the late senator, now moves to the House of Representatives.\n*   **U.S. Economic Data:** Financial markets are reacting to a Labor Department report showing **unexpected job losses** in July, leading to revised expectations for Federal Reserve interest rate hikes.\n*   **Thailand School Shooting:** The death toll from a school shooting in Thailand has risen to nine following the death of a 12-year-old girl in the hospital.",
